 "contract": {
  "id": "t5_seq_detector",
  "title": "serial pattern detector (1011, overlapping)",
  "tier": "T5",
  "description": "Build a serial pattern detector. DIN is the data lever and CLK the clock lever. On every rising edge of CLK (switched ON) the circuit takes in the value DIN had just before the edge. The lamp MATCH is lit exactly while the last four bits taken in were 1, 0, 1, 1 (oldest first; overlapping matches count: 1011011 matches twice). Before four bits have been taken in, the missing older bits count as 0, so MATCH is off at the start. Switching CLK off changes nothing. DIN is changed at least 14 ticks before an edge; CLK stays on and off for at least 20 ticks each. Library hint (component tier only): D flip-flop and NOT gate cells are available.",
